{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Usability in System Design  "}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about system usability."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Interprets the technical design report, to determine the work plan during the phase of building the software, based on regulation ad protocols established by the company.  Designs the graphic layout of the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level. Exchanges simple information on the graphic layout of an IT solution, functional requirements of a business through the IT solution, and the functional phase of an IT project."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find information about how to develop usability when designing a graphic layout."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose the most important information in bullet points. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a piece of cardboard, design a graphic layout and write the most important aspects you include to develop usability on it. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the layout with the whole class. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Give an oral presentation to explain to your partners about how you developed usability in the graphic design.  "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find information about how to develop usability when designing a graphic layout. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I choose the most important information. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a layout with the most important aspects to develop usability. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain to my partners how to develop usability in a graphic design. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "survey "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a series of questions that attempt to find out specific information "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Juan, according to the users' survey we implemented in the web page about its usability, we had better change some aspects to make it more user friendly.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "usable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "ready for use"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How are we going to make sure that the new design is usable?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "user-friendly "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that is easy to be used"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I thought this web page had all the necessary attributes to be user friendly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "arrangement "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fix or organize something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At the end, if they don't develop those tasks, we will analyze data and we will make the necessary arrangements in the design."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "optimize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make effective something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: So, is there a way to optimize time?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "field study "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a study done under certain characteristics  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Then, we need to have a field study; to check the users' behaviors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le03ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Simple- Negative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are many tenses that can be used to talk about actions in the future. One of such tenses is the <span class =\"strong\">present simple</span>. You can use the present simple to talk about actions that take place in the future. These actions can or cannot take place, this is why, we are to focus on the negative form of this tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To talk about the future with <span class =\"strong\">present simple</span>, you just need to device a sentence using this tense and add an adverb that points out that the action is taking place in a time beyond the present. Take a look at the structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Simple present</span> </br></br> Pronoun + Verb + Complement </br></br>Example: </br> <span class =\"italic\">You <span class =\"strong\">need</span> to come to the design test <span class =\"strong\">tomorrow morning</span>. It's mandatory!</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Structure: </br> Pronoun + Will + Verb + Complement </br> Example: </br>I will create a new design."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now, as it was pointed out above, the actions may not need to be performed, nevertheless, they are suggested as a negative possibility in the future. Take a look at the structure:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Simple present in negative</span></br></br> Pronoun + Aux (do/does) + Not + Verb + Complement  </br></br>Example: </br> <span class =\"italic\">You <span class =\"strong\">don't need</span> to come to the design test <span class =\"strong\">tomorrow morning</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We don't have a meeting tomorrow, but we have it this very afternoon!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We have a usability testing session tomorrow to make sure that users don't have any problem using the page in the near future. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Importance of Usability"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Useless systems usually end up in high costs to the business; clients' satisfaction and productivity are the most affected aspects. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most important aspect of a system usability is that clients will be able to complete their tasks effectively, which gives them a sense of satisfaction when manipulating a computer. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some negative aspects about usability are:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<li>People will never use a system if they find it difficult to use. </li> <li>People will search elsewhere for products or information if it is not easy to do it in your web page. </li> <li>People won't like to spend lots of time trying to find information. </li> <li>People won't like to contact for support if they find the system inappropriate. </li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that designing a usable system doesn't depend on the designer only, clients play an important role when designing systems too, because identifying their needs play an important role in a system's design. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "First of all, we are going to have a usability testing session to make sure that users in the future will have no problems using the page."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, we ought to create a series of tasks that users need to develop without any help. While they develop those tasks, we are taking notes about their behavior and time they take to complete tasks. At the end, if they don't develop those tasks in the projected time, we will analyze data and we will make the necessary arrangements in the design."}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class =\"strong\">Camila: </span>Juan, according to the users' survey we implemented in the web page regarding its usability, we had better change some aspects to make it more user friendly.</br><span class =\"strong\">Juan: </span>I see. According to the results, this web page doesn't have all the necessary attributes to be user friendly yet. Although, our designer seems to have included everything for that purpose.</br><span class =\"strong\">Camila: </span>Well, it looks like we don't have a meeting tomorrow, but we have it this very afternoon! The designer doesn't know very well what usability is and the design he created was not a user-centered design.</br><span class =\"strong\">Juan: </span>How are we going to make sure the new design is usable?</div>"}, {"time": "40000", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class =\"strong\">Camila:</span> I consider that we might want to implement a testing process; we have a usability testing session next week to make sure that users don't have any problem using the page in the near future. We ought to create a series of tasks that users need to develop without any help. While they develop those tasks, we take notes on their behavior and the time they take to complete tasks. At the end, if they don't develop those tasks in the projected time, we will analyze data and we will make the necessary arrangements in the design.</br><span class =\"strong\">Juan:</span> I imagine that once we've finished with all the tests, we'll have lots of changes in the design. So, is there a way to optimize time?</br><span class =\"strong\">Camila: </span>Well, we might want to work on usability.</div>"}, {"time": "82000", "image": "enpe8n5le03ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class =\"strong\">Juan: </span>How are we going to do that?</br><span class =\"strong\">Camila:</span> First, we need to test the previous design during the next weeks to check all the things that we don't need. Then, we need to have a field study to check the users' behaviors. We might want to create paper prototypes to test them. After that, we ought to create multiple iterations on the computer to check which one works best. Then, we implement the final design. This means that we don't have to focus on time, but also on usability in this afternoon's meeting.</br></div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le03ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe8n5le03ob03re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the importance of usability in graphic design. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe how to develop usability when designing a system."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you make sure a system is usable?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think the steps to make a system usable are?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type"